A||||3||MooCow||I found another Fiero! What would you do?||||6||
Z||000000||MooCow||03-15-2000||08:42 AM||||Well I found another Fiero. It is an 86 SE v6 with 93,000 miles, all gold and looks to be in good shape.  It even comes with a 6 months 7,500 mile warrenty.  The thing is they are asking 2,700 for it.  Is this to much?  I know that they said that it has a leak in the exhaust system.  Also the front end looks like a different color than the rest of the car.  It almost looks like it had a bra on and the dealer took it off, or the paint is only faded in that spot.  Should I go for it?  Remember this will be my first Feiro as long as insurance isn't to much and if I can convince my parents.<BR>                           Thanks Ken||||reg||6
Z||000001||Oreif||03-15-2000||11:29 AM||||It sounds like it's at a dealership. I would test drive it and give it a good once over. If it is in good shape (other rhan the faded nose) I'd tell them $2000.00 "out the door"<BR>They probably only gave the person who traded it in $1200 to $1400 (Kelly black book trade-in price) Who knows maybe even less.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GT Bastard||03-15-2000||12:01 PM||||That exhuast leak is likely on the manifold(not fun to fix.)  I would try to get them to fix the leak before you go for it.  Or you could just bring it back under warranty and tell them the exhaust leaks.  hehe.... Why would they sell you a car with a warranty, and then tell about a problem it has?  Anyhow, the price isn't too shocking, but I'm sure they'd take less.||||reg||1
Z||000003||RFMike||03-15-2000||11:27 PM||||When I see contrasting color in body parts, I immediately think replacement parts.  This car may have had front end damage, and a different facia put on.  This could be a very minor issue, as the only damage might have been to the facia.  However, I would get a good body shop to look at the frame for damage.  If there is spaceframe damage, stay away from it, unless your body shop says they can fix it, and you can believe them.  Then the damage is a major bargaining chip.<BR>If everything is ok, the price is still at the high end.  If this is a dealership, they will definitely come down.<BR>Good luck<BR>Mike||||reg||1
